WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.178 --> 00:00:03.302
-You're always so fun,
and I love when you're funny.

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:05.871
And we always joke around
every time you're here.

00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:08.841
But this movie, "Fatherhood,"
is a beautiful story.

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:13.079
-It's based on a true story of
a guy named Matt Logelin.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:17.283
And the story is about
a man whose life

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.684
got flipped upside down.

00:00:18.684 --> 00:00:21.387
You know, he lost his wife
after delivering a baby

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:28.895
and was left with, you know, the
idea of raising a child

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.731
by himself
after suffering, you know,

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:35.634
one of the darkest moments
in his life.

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:38.437
And there was a high level of
doubt in what he could do,

00:00:38.437 --> 00:00:41.574
if he could do, and rather than
giving up, you know,

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:45.311
he had to figure out a way
to kind of bear down

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:48.481
and stick with what life
has thrown at him

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:50.216
and make the best of it.

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:54.020
And in this case,
for me to take on the role,

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.621
it gave me the opportunity
to show a black father

00:00:55.621 --> 00:00:56.822
in a positive light.

00:00:56.822 --> 00:01:00.659
You know, for some time on
the screen, on TV,

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:04.697
if we're not getting out of jail
or on drugs or off drugs --

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.999
You know,
there's a significant struggle

00:01:06.999 --> 00:01:08.902
behind the image
of a black father.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.470
And I said,
"This is an opportunity

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.040
just to put it in
the space of positivity."

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.676
And that was my reason
for taking on the role

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:19.411
and also challenging
myself to --

00:01:19.411 --> 00:01:20.913
you know, to go a little
deeper into acting.

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:22.281
It's a serious story.

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:25.218
It's emotional.
And it has its waves.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.952
So I'm excited about the journey

00:01:26.952 --> 00:01:28.288
that I'm about to
take my audience on.

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:30.323
-Your co-star in the movie
is a baby.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:33.459
Now, clearly,
you can't use an actual baby

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:35.295
for all the hours of filming.

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:38.164
So you had a --
-Says who?

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.165
Says who?

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.934
-No, no, that's a fact.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.101
-No, it's not.
-Yes, it is.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:43.502
-No, it's not a fact.
-Yes, it is a fact.

00:01:43.502 --> 00:01:46.138
-We had a brilliant baby --
we had a brilliant baby

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:48.841
that I worked with,
and this baby was relentless.

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:51.110
This baby worked hours.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.246
Hours. This baby was pulling
14-hour days.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.247
-No, no, no. That is not true.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.015
-I've never seen
anything like it.

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:58.017
-No, Kevin,
that was a fake baby.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:00.520
I know this for a fact --
that you are not allowed to work

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.354
for this many hours with a baby.

00:02:02.354 --> 00:02:04.590
What you were acting with
was a doll.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:05.591
-This is ridiculous!

00:02:05.591 --> 00:02:07.727
What you're saying
is ridiculous!

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:12.097
To say that I would work with --
As a thesbian.

00:02:12.097 --> 00:02:13.266
I'm a thesbian.

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.534
To suggest that I would work --
-Thespian.

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.770
Thespian, not a thesbian.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.439
-Don't you tell me -- Don't you
tell me what it is.

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:22.775
For you to suggest that,
you've got some nerve, Jimmy,

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:25.245
to think that that was
a fake baby.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:28.014
You better look at the tape.
I only work with real babies.

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.648
It's in my contract, buddy.

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:32.085
I'm Kevin "The Real Baby
Work-with-er" Hart.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.186
That's who I am.

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:35.221
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.993
That's who I am.

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:43.162
That's who I am, Jimmy, okay?

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:44.563
-I want to say
you did a great job

00:02:44.563 --> 00:02:45.965
in this film, by the way.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.566
I did see it,
and you were great.

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:49.368
And I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:51.470
Here is Kevin Hart
in "Fatherhood."

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:52.539
Take a look at this.

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:54.040
-I don't know
if it's normal or not,

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.174
but it's two different kinds.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:56.709
She can either hit you
with a streamer --

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.444
that's when
it's all put together

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:01.547
and it's a little solid and
it's a direct hit --

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:04.550
or she'll buckshot you,
and that's -- that's that spay.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.619
It's a quick whop.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.087
I need help.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:11.090
I need the crying to stop.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:14.327
How do I make the crying stop?

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:15.728
-Okay.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:18.064
Um, my oldest had colic for
the first couple of months.

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:19.499
-What's colic?

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:23.169
-It's when babies cry for hours
on end without any reason,

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:26.606
till you feel like your eyes
are about to pop out.

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.040
-I gave the baby colic.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.109
-No, that's -- that's not
how colic works.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:31.643
-It's 'cause I'm not
washing my hands

00:03:31.643 --> 00:03:32.745
and I'm just touching the baby.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.447
That's how I gave the baby
colic, probably.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:36.215
-You don't give a baby colic.

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:38.317
It's more of a digestive thing.

00:03:38.317 --> 00:03:43.022
-That's a relief.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.924
-Kevin Hart, everybody!

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.225
That's how you do it
right there.

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:50.963
"Fatherhood" begins streaming
on Netflix on June 18th.

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:55.234
Pre-order his book,
"Marcus Makes a Movie."

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:56.269
Thank you again for being here.

